------------------------------------------------------------
ALGORITHM PROGRAMS
------------------------------------------------------------
bubble.asm       bubble sort of {5,3,8,1,4}  -> 1 3 4 5 8
insertion.asm    insertion sort              -> 1 3 4 5 8
selection.asm    selection sort              -> 1 3 4 5 8
max_element.asm  maximum of the same array   -> 8 stored in "maxval"
All four assemble, run to HALT and give the results above (see the
memory dump at the end of each .log file, run with a dump size of 128).
They keep every address in a local variable because SIMPLEX only has the
two-register stack A and B.

